WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.300
It never hurts to plan ahead — especially
when it comes to Hollywood’s biggest flicks!

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:11.290
From long-awaited sequels to an animated musical
reboot, these are the 2025 movies worth making

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:13.730
some room on your calendar for!

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:18.740
Originally intended for release in November
of 2024, Marvel Studios' "Fantastic Four"

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.630
reboot has been pushed back to February 14,
2025.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:27.880
The long-awaited project is set to be one
of the first films of the MCU's Phase 6, which

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:32.009
will also include two "Avengers" films — but
more on that later.

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:36.660
In September of 2022, Deadline reported that
Jeff Kaplan and Ian Springer had been brought

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.309
on to write the screenplay for the film, with
Matt Shakman directing.

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:44.510
While Springer and Kaplan haven't had a ton
of high-profile work go up in Hollywood yet,

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:49.649
Shakman is an experienced TV director with
episodes of "Fargo," "Game of Thrones," and

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.870
"It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia" on his
resume.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:56.760
He's worked with Marvel Studios before, having
directed and executive produced the first

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:00.760
Marvel Disney+ series, "WandaVision," in 2021.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:05.119
Few story details have been released about
the new "Fantastic Four," but as always, there

00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:07.790
are some clues as to what fans can expect.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.720
For one, Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige
has suggested that he wants to avoid a traditional

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.080
origin story, considering how many times "The
Fantastic Four" has been adapted for the big

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.290
screen since the turn of the century.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.299
"This is the story that Kevin wants."

00:01:21.299 --> 00:01:25.210
"Okay, then I wanna talk to Kevin."

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.710
[laughter]

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:31.790
Popular fancast John Krasinski has already
played a version of Reed Richards in "Doctor

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:35.850
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness," but
the actor has stated that he isn't necessarily

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:37.950
planning on returning.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:42.990
There was a time when the whole point of an
MCU movie was to help build up to a new entry

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:48.040
in "The Avengers" series — but ever since
Iron Man snapped his fingers and turned Thanos

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.430
into dust back in 2019, that hasn't been the
case.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:55.939
By the time "Avengers: The Kang Dynasty" is
released in 2025 — currently scheduled for

00:01:55.939 --> 00:02:01.695
May 2 — the MCU will have gone two entire
phases without an entry in "The Avengers" saga.

00:02:01.695 --> 00:02:07.220
That should be enough to build plenty of excitement
for the series' fifth installment, but there

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:10.050
are plenty of other reasons to look forward
to it.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:14.160
"Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings"
director Destin Daniel Cretton is set to direct

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.170
"The Kang Dynasty," with Jeff Loveness writing
the script.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:21.730
Loveness, who comes from a background writing
for comedy shows like "Jimmy Kimmel Live!"

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:26.160
and "Rick and Morty," also penned the screenplay
for "Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania," which

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.120
brings Kang the Conqueror to the MCU for the
first time.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:34.410
As such, he seems like a perfect choice to
write "Avengers 5," and it's likely that the

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:37.380
Phase 5 film will set up a lot.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:42.450
As of now, all we know about "The Kang Dynasty"
is that it will star the titular time-traveling

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:47.920
villain, who seems ready to usurp Thanos'
throne as the MCU's scariest antagonist.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:53.390
The comic run from which the film takes its
title may offer some clues: in it, Kang successfully

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:59.160
takes over the entire world, bringing unparalleled
destruction and terror along the way.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.560
The Avengers will definitely have their hands
full in Phase 6.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.530
"See you soon."

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:12.340
The all-star horror movie team of James Wan,
Jason Blum, and Akela Cooper united to release

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:18.395
"M3GAN" in early 2023 — a surprise hit about
a young girl's robotic companion who turns murderous.

00:03:18.395 --> 00:03:24.430
Directed by Gerard Johnstone, the film grossed
nearly $175 million at the global box office

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:30.610
on a budget of just $12 million, sparking
rumors of a sequel that has since been confirmed.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:36.810
According to Deadline, "M3GAN 2.0" is planned
for release on January 17, 2025.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:41.780
Original stars Allison Williams and Violet
McGraw are both set to return, with Williams

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.689
stepping into a full producer role as well.

00:03:44.689 --> 00:03:49.934
In an interview with New Zealand's 1 News,
Johnstone said he's in talks to return as director.

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:54.120
While we don't have any leads on story details
yet, it's not hard to imagine where "M3GAN

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.390
2.0" might go.

00:03:55.390 --> 00:04:01.250
The first film ends on a victorious, but ominous
note that ensures viewers know that the titular

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.459
M3GAN is far from dead.

00:04:03.459 --> 00:04:07.909
Given the sci-fi trappings of the franchise,
there are any number of ways she could return

00:04:07.909 --> 00:04:11.110
— bigger, scarier, and deadlier.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:16.000
Cooper returns to pen the script while both
Blum and Wan are set to act as producers,

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.269
which means that it's safe to assume that
the sequel will have the same overall feel

00:04:20.269 --> 00:04:21.269
as the original.

00:04:21.269 --> 00:04:25.711
In an interview with Collider, Wan said he
already has ideas for a "bigger world" for

00:04:25.711 --> 00:04:26.759
the series.

00:04:26.759 --> 00:04:30.039
Could this be the start of the next hit horror
franchise?

00:04:30.039 --> 00:04:31.680
Only time will tell.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:37.759
In early 2021, fans of "Avatar: The Last Airbender"
rejoiced at the announcement of Avatar Studios,

00:04:37.759 --> 00:04:43.590
a new division of Paramount+ and Nickelodeon
fully focused on developing the beloved franchise.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:48.120
Original series creators Bryan Konietzko and
Michael Dante DiMartino will serve as chief

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:53.120
creative officers for the studio's first animated
film intended for theatrical release.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:58.230
Over a year later, Nickelodeon teased — through
Avatar Korra voice actor Janet Varney — that

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:01.330
the film would follow "Avatar Aang and his
friends."

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:06.610
In November of 2022, a release date of October
10, 2025, was announced.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:11.000
No other story details have been confirmed,
but given the recent history of the "Avatar"

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.110
franchise, we can assume a few things.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:17.400
The official comics from Dark Horse take place
in the immediate aftermath of the original

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:22.389
show's finale, and it seems unlikely that
the movie — the franchise's triumphant return

00:05:22.389 --> 00:05:25.600
to animation — would simply recycle those
stories.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:31.150
Plus, the original voice cast is grown up
now, and Zach Tyler Eisen, the actor behind

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:34.139
Aang, doesn't really do voice-over work anymore.

00:05:34.139 --> 00:05:38.620
For these reasons, it might make more sense
for the film to follow adult versions of the

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:43.560
"Avatar: The Last Airbender" characters with
either new voice actors or the ones used for

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.520
flashbacks in "The Legend of Korra."

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:47.100
"Well, that's just silly.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.080
I don't sound like that!"

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:53.080
"Oh man, this writer's a genius!"

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.990
Either way, the film definitely sounds promising.

00:05:55.990 --> 00:06:00.830
In addition to Konietzko and DiMartino, longtime
franchise director Lauren Montgomery is helming

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:06.157
the project, and the versatile Australian
animation studio Flying Bark Productions will produce.

00:06:06.157 --> 00:06:10.520
Hopefully things go better than the last time
Aang and his friends hit cinemas.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:15.060
The past few years have been rough for "Star
Wars" on the big screen.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:19.610
After the lackluster responses to "Solo: A
Star Wars Story" and "Star Wars: The Rise

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:24.610
of Skywalker," Disney officially declared
a "hiatus" on its planned slate of future

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:29.430
films, deciding to focus instead on building
out the franchise on Disney+ instead.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:34.819
For a time, "Star Wars" was set to return
to theaters in 2023, with Patty Jenkins' "Rogue

00:06:34.819 --> 00:06:36.979
Squadron" movie looking like the likely choice.

00:06:36.979 --> 00:06:41.949
However, Jenkins' film has been temporarily
derailed, with Lucasfilm president Kathleen

00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:45.849
Kennedy telling Vanity Fair in 2022 that it
was undergoing rewrites.

00:06:45.849 --> 00:06:51.300
As of now, a "Star Wars" movie is still slated
for release in December of 2025, but it's

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.410
hard to predict what it will be.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:57.290
Numerous projects have been rumored over the
past few years, including potential films

00:06:57.290 --> 00:07:01.960
from Taika Waititi, "Stranger Things" producer
Shawn Levy, and "Star Trek Into Darkness"

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:02.960
writer Damon Lindelof.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:07.840
A story from The Hollywood Reporter in October
of 2022 claimed that Lindelof's film may be

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:12.860
the next one up in 2025 — and that a writer's
room has already assembled at Lucasfilm to

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.090
work on ideas.

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:18.310
It's clear that Disney is experimenting with
many different ideas, which makes it hard

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:19.949
to predict what we'll get next.

00:07:19.949 --> 00:07:24.150
At the very least, Lucasfilm doesn't seem
to be lacking ideas.

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:29.670
Kennedy told Total Film in 2022 that she wants
to create "a whole new saga," and there have

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:34.110
been reports of both a "Knights of the Old
Republic" project and more movies set in the

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:35.110
sequel era.

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:39.900
Whatever happens, the return of "Star Wars"
to the big screen is an exciting prospect

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:40.900
for fans.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:45.610
It may feel strange if you grew up watching
"SpongeBob SquarePants" on Nickelodeon, but

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:50.699
the animated undersea comedy franchise is
now nearly as prolific on the big screen as

00:07:50.699 --> 00:07:51.699
the small.

00:07:51.699 --> 00:07:56.550
The series first made its way to theaters
with 2004's "The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie,"

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:59.539
which carried the same core animation style
as the show.

00:07:59.539 --> 00:08:04.840
Over a decade passed before the next big-screen
outing, 2015's "The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:07.539
Out of Water," which became a huge success.

00:08:07.539 --> 00:08:12.229
"The SpongeBob Movie: Sponge on the Run,"
followed in 2020, and another film in the

00:08:12.229 --> 00:08:16.009
modern 3D style has been announced for May
23, 2025.

00:08:16.009 --> 00:08:20.400
Nickelodeon hasn't revealed any real details
of what the story will entail, and with the

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:24.550
franchise now more expansive than ever, the
possibilities are endless.

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:29.300
"SpongeBob SquarePants" has become a major
IP asset for Paramount in the company's modern

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:34.580
hybrid release era, with the movies supplementing
multiple series across both traditional television

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:37.440
and streaming distribution on Paramount+.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:41.940
It could even be said that the studio is overloaded
with "SpongeBob SquarePants" content, but

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:44.649
it still shows no signs of slowing down.

00:08:44.649 --> 00:08:49.940
"Sponge Out of Water" was a box office hit
and received strong reviews, but "Sponge on

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:53.910
the Run" was met with a much more lukewarm
reception a few years later.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:55.830
"Hey now, buck up! 

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.709
It's, it's not over yet, SpongeBob!"

00:08:58.709 --> 00:09:01.589
"It sure feels over… and crappy!"

00:09:01.589 --> 00:09:05.709
It remains to be seen if the third film of
this modern series will continue a decline

00:09:05.709 --> 00:09:08.450
or return to the franchise's former peaks.

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:10.600
With some luck, it will be the latter.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:15.990
"A Quiet Place" has become one of the biggest
surprises in recent movie history, growing

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:21.820
from a one-off horror movie made on a $17
million budget to a blockbuster franchise.

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:26.120
The creative collaboration between real-life
couple John Krasinski and Emily Blunt was

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:31.079
a standout hit, and a spin-off film set before
the events of the original is set for release

00:09:31.079 --> 00:09:32.430
in 2024.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:35.861
Those who want the proper conclusion to the
story of the Abbott family, however, will

00:09:35.861 --> 00:09:37.950
have to wait until 2025.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:42.870
Blunt has been open for some time about the
original story being intended as a trilogy,

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:47.310
which suggests that "A Quiet Place: Part III"
will wrap up the major character arcs that

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:48.790
began in 2018.

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:53.100
In early 2022, Krasinski declared a 2025 release
for the threequel.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.779
Presumably, he will be directing once again.

00:09:55.779 --> 00:09:59.921
With a full-on prequel set to release before
"A Quiet Place: Part III" comes out, there

00:09:59.921 --> 00:10:03.910
could be a lot of new elements added to the
hit horror saga.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:08.461
That should make the eventual conclusion even
more exciting — but for now, details are

00:10:08.461 --> 00:10:10.380
being kept under wraps.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:14.500
After a somewhat confused period for the Caped
Crusader's film career following Christopher

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:19.040
Nolan's "The Dark Knight" trilogy, director
Matt Reeves and star Robert Pattinson returned

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:22.180
Bruce Wayne to his former glory with "The
Batman."

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:28.040
The 2022 film received excellent reviews and
performed well at the box office, succeeding

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:33.110
on the merits of its gritty, noir-inspired
tone and stellar production design.

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:37.410
It wasn't long before a proper sequel was
announced, with Pattinson and Reeves both

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:41.260
returning along with "Project Power" writer
Mattson Tomlin on scripting duty.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:44.380
The film is set to release on October 3, 2025.

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:49.970
"The Batman" has already done an excellent
job of building out a distinct version of

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:55.366
Gotham City, and it's easy to imagine all
kinds of directions in which the sequel could go.

00:10:55.366 --> 00:11:00.110
Pattinson himself told Den of Geek in 2022
that he'd be interested in a version of the

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:04.779
popular Court of Owls storyline, while Reeves
has expressed interest in a "grounded version"

00:11:04.779 --> 00:11:06.150
of Mr. Freeze.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:10.750
It's also likely that Barry Keoghan's Joker,
who debuted at the end of "The Batman," could

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:12.320
play a major role.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:16.690
There's even the possibility that we haven't
yet seen the last of Paul Dano's Riddler.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:18.760
"And you know…

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:22.209
Gotham loves a comeback story."

00:11:22.209 --> 00:11:28.110
Gotham City has a nearly endless trove of
bad guys to pull from, and Reeves has proved

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:33.900
himself a very competent filmmaker with both
"The Batman" and other projects like the latter-day

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:35.389
"Planet of the Apes" movies.

00:11:35.389 --> 00:11:40.420
Wherever his team decides to take the story,
it should be exciting to watch.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:44.950
The Smurfs haven't had the steadiest track
record at the modern box office, with Sony

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:49.260
Pictures' 2010s film series receiving poor
reviews throughout its run.

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:53.860
In 2022, it was announced that Nickelodeon
and Paramount would be putting their own spin

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:59.510
on the classic franchise with an animated
musical film scheduled for release in 2024.

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:05.336
That date was later pushed to February 14,
2025 to make room for "Sonic the Hedgehog 3."

00:12:05.336 --> 00:12:09.490
As you might expect, the upcoming reboot is
intended to be a family film with plenty of

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:11.920
cartoon whimsy and musical charm.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:15.750
Chris Miller has been tapped to direct the
picture — he's quite experienced in the

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:20.250
genre, having previously helmed the DreamWorks
Animation features "Shrek the Third" and "Puss

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:21.250
in Boots."

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:25.710
There's been little in the way of official
casting news, but it seems safe to assume

00:12:25.710 --> 00:12:30.380
that the new "Smurfs" film will follow the
modern Hollywood trend of casting an ensemble

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:33.230
of recognizable stars to play the various
roles.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:39.209
Hopefully, Paramount can finally do the brand
justice and properly relaunch "The Smurfs"

00:12:39.209 --> 00:12:40.500
for a new generation.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:44.190
The "Tron" franchise is one of Disney's oddest.

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:50.060
The original 1982 film wasn't exactly a box
office smash, but it developed a cult appeal

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:54.480
thanks to its groundbreaking CGI effects — a
rare sight at the time.

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:59.920
A sequel, "Tron: Legacy," followed in 2010,
but momentum stalled on any further development

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.461
of the franchise.

00:13:01.461 --> 00:13:05.570
Now, a third film, currently going by the
name of "Tron: Ares," is finally back on the

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:09.760
books with Jared Leto set to star and Joachim
Rønning directing.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:12.949
The movie is currently expected on December
19, 2025.

00:13:12.949 --> 00:13:18.209
Under Rønning's direction, it could be quite
a spectacle: the filmmaker is no stranger

00:13:18.209 --> 00:13:23.180
to the contemporary live-action Disney blockbuster
machine, having previously helmed films like

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:28.190
"Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Men Tell No
Tales" in 2017 and "Maleficent: Mistress of

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:29.790
Evil" in 2019.

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:34.930
Leto may be less of a sure thing, as he's
developed a reputation for box office bombs

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:37.630
in addition to his questionable on-set behavior.

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:42.680
Regardless, a return to the digital grid of
"Tron" with today's advancements in computer

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:45.500
animation technology is an exciting idea.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:50.170
The series has always been more about a certain
look and feel than a hard-hitting narrative,

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:53.630
and it's likely that this trend will continue
into the future.

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:57.959
Maybe Disney can even get Daft Punk back together
to do the soundtrack again — but we're not

00:13:57.959 --> 00:13:59.699
getting our hopes up that high.

00:13:59.699 --> 00:14:02.602
"This is going to be quite a ride."

